<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Boot loader (THEME_PLAN §13.5, P8e)

    The Méthode mark building itself, shown in the gap between the backend HTML
    arriving and OWL mounting the webclient.  On a cold bundle that gap is
    seconds long, and until now it was a blank page — the screen a prospect sees
    immediately after logging in.

    ⚠ WHY THIS IS SERVER-SIDE QWEB AND NOT AN OWL TEMPLATE.  It has to paint
    BEFORE any JavaScript runs; an OWL component cannot, by definition, render
    during the wait for OWL.

    ⚠ THE CSS IS NOT HERE, AND INLINING IT DOES NOT MAKE THE MARK PAINT SOONER.
    That was tried and reverted; do not try it again without re-reading this.
    web.layout emits web.assets_web as a render-blocking <link> (1,031,289 bytes
    on this build), and a blocking stylesheet gates the first paint no matter
    what follows it in <head> — so an inline <style> after that link buys exactly
    zero milliseconds while creating a second home for the tree's styling.

    The floor on "when does the loader appear" is therefore: HTML round trip
    (~50ms local) + download and parse of that megabyte.  Moving it earlier means
    making Odoo's own stylesheet non-render-blocking, which trades this delay for
    a flash of unstyled webclient — a real decision, not a tweak, and not one to
    take silently.

    Styling lives in static/src/scss/loader.scss with the snackbar.

    ⚠ WHY THE SVG IS INLINE.  Per-shape animation is the whole asset — nine nodes
    and ten edges enter on their own delays.  An <img> or a background url()
    renders SVG in an isolated context outside CSS cannot reach, so the mark
    would appear fully built and static.  It must be real DOM.

    The 19 path definitions are byte-identical to the brand source at
    static/description/brand/building-tree-seamless.html; only the class names
    are prefixed, so nothing here can collide with an Odoo selector.  Geometry is
    not hand-maintained — regenerate from that file rather than editing.

    ⚠ EVERY ANIMATION DELAY IS A FRACTION OF THE CYCLE, not an absolute number
    of seconds — see loader.scss.  The brand asset hardcodes .32s/.64s/1.26s
    against a 3.6s cycle, so shortening the cycle there would desynchronise the
    build from the teardown.
-->
<odoo>

    <template id="webclient_bootstrap_boot_loader" inherit_id="web.webclient_bootstrap">
        <!--
            web.layout renders `<body t-att-class="body_classname"><t t-out="0"/></body>`,
            so the default slot of this t-call IS the body.  Its existing children
            are all t-set and emit nothing, which is why appending here puts the
            loader alone in the body until the webclient mounts over it.
        -->
        <xpath expr="//t[@t-call='web.layout']" position="inside">
            <div id="m-boot-loader" class="m-boot-loader">
